1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,426
<i>The martial law troops</i>
<i>have completed an operation</i>

3
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>to clear out the rioters</i>
<i>who resisted to the very end.</i>

4
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,847
<i>The rioters have been suppressed.</i>

5
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:59,559
<i>Rioters, surrender and lay down</i>
<i>your weapons, and you will be spared.</i>

6
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:02,103
<i>If you refuse to do so,</i>
<i>you will be shot dead.</i>

7
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,480
<i>We warn you once again.</i>

8
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,440
<i>The rioters have been suppressed.</i>

9
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>Lay down your weapons and surrender.</i>

10
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,944
<i>Those who resist will all be shot dead.</i>

11
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:43,163
JI DU-SEOK

12
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:47,709
PATIENT: JI DU-SEOK
PRIMARY: KIM HYEON-MIN

13
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:54,841
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

14
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,510
EPISODE 7

15
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:07,312
- No!
- Mr. Oh!

16
00:03:20,658 --> 00:03:22,327
Heard you had a rough night?

17
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:25,163
Did you see?

18
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:27,373
- See what?
- That VIP guy.

19
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,458
Why do you ask?

20
00:03:28,541 --> 00:03:30,585
'Cause I'm curious, obviously!

21
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:32,587
I heard he's aged a ton.

22
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,505
Myocardial infarction, huh?

23
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:37,717
As always, I guess you really never know
when someone's time is up.

24
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,594
Just last year, he was spry as ever,

25
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:42,722
blathering at a golf course
about how "history will be the judge!",

26
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,515
and speeding off in his golf cart.

27
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:45,725
- I'm heading inside.
- Oh, hey.

28
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:47,685
Uh, that patient, Oh Sang-beom,

29
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,562
did he pull that knowing
the VIP'd be here?

30
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,606
- Huh? After seeing the news?
- It wasn't that.

31
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:55,401
Want me to switch you out?
Someone else is available now.

32
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:57,237
All right, all right.

33
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,906
I was just making
small-talk to loosen us up for surgery.

34
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,533
Hey, how is he? Mr. Oh Sang-beom.

35
00:04:03,868 --> 00:04:05,453
VIP WARD

36
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,414
- Mr. Oh, calm down!
- Don't leave me!

37
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:09,832
Do it, shoot it now!

38
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:11,709
You're in the hospital.

39
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:14,545
You're in the hospital.
It's okay. You're okay, sir.

40
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:15,964
Calm down. Calm, please.

41
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:18,383
- Please, just… Oh, Christ…
- Get away!

42
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,969
You're okay, sir.
It's okay, you're all right.

43
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,904
What could he possibly be dreaming about

44
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:43,658
that leaves him neither entirely asleep,
nor entirely awake, either?

45
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:46,160
You think he's ever gotten
a good night's sleep in all these years?

46
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,375
So, this is how it must've felt.

47
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,545
In what way?

48
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,839
Back then.

49
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,844
Like, way back then.

50
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:04,470
- No!
- Oh, Su-jeong!

51
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,891
- Su-jeong!
- Su-jeong!

52
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:10,935
- Su-jeong, it's okay.
- Su-jeong! I'm here.

53
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:12,895
- It's okay. You're at home.
- I'm here.

54
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:27,035
- Here. You all should eat, dig in.
- Thank you.

55
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,329
I'm sorry, um, right now, I'm not hungry--

56
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,663
Thanks for the food.

57
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:35,168
Is this what Doctor Woo Jae-gyeong
gave us before?

58
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:37,920
Ah!

59
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:40,256
Eat it with <i>gejang</i>, too.
There's really no better way to eat it.

60
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,716
- Oh…
- It's the stuff.

61
00:05:42,675 --> 00:05:44,761
- Don't be shy, try a spoonful. Go on.
- Okay.

62
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:49,223
It's actually really good.

63
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:53,394
Ugh. I just wish Mr. Oh was
able to have some with us, too.

64
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:55,104
Well, if his condition stabilizes,

65
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:57,565
they could move him
to a different floor, it's only that…

66
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:01,486
Apparently, they discussed

67
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:03,321
transferring him in their meeting.

68
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,491
So, the surgery's canceled?

69
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:07,909
The hospital is giving up on him?

70
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:11,371
What… That's ridiculous. Why would
the hospital transfer Mr. Oh out?

71
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,872
Out of anybody, that guy should go.

72
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:14,040
Thanks again for the food.

73
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,876
Doctor Woo Jae-gyeong's coming to visit.

74
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:19,796
He planned to come right away, but
he couldn't get time off from the clinic.

75
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,090
He's requesting a discharge.

76
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:27,053
He says this's too cruel and that
he wants to take him back home.

77
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:34,143
Apologize! Apologize!

78
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:37,146
- Down with Ji Du-seok!
- Down with him!

79
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,481
Down with him!

80
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:40,817
- Ji Du-seok must…
- Apologize!

81
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,902
Apologize! Apologize!

82
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,445
- Down with Ji Du-seok!
- Down with him!

83
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,030
- Excuse me, sorry, excuse me.
- Down with him!

84
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,281
Excuse me. Sorry, my bad.

85
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:49,534
- Uh, sir, let's go this way.
- Ji Du-seok must…

86
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:51,619
- Apologize! Apologize!
- Incoming. Excuse us, sorry!

87
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:53,037
- Down with Ji Du-seok!
- Sorry.

88
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:55,498
Down with him!

89
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:58,626
- Ms. Jang, Ms. Jang!
- Mr. Oh!

90
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,795
Mr. Oh, can you hear me?

91
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:01,879
I got you.

92
00:07:03,005 --> 00:07:04,006
It's okay, you're okay.

93
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:07,677
<i>That day, Sang-beom</i>
<i>went looking for his brother,</i>

94
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:11,055
<i>and somehow made it all the way</i>
<i>to the provincial government office.</i>

95
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:14,976
<i>And, apparently, along with</i>
<i>his classmates from night school,</i>

96
00:07:15,059 --> 00:07:16,936
<i>Seung-beom happened to be there,</i>

97
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:20,148
<i>along with his cousin,</i>
<i>as well as his uncle</i>

98
00:07:20,731 --> 00:07:22,567
<i>and a female restaurant owner.</i>

99
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:25,278
How'd that kid manage to
drag this all the way by himself?

100
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,363
- Hey, look up at me.
- Poor kid,

101
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,699
he was dead set on finding his brother.

102
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,791
Eat this.

103
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:43,171
<i>He was shoveling the rice ball</i>
<i>into his mouth with one hand,</i>

104
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:45,006
<i>- holding onto his brother with the other…</i>
- Eat slowly.

105
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,842
<i>- …afraid he might lose him…</i>
- He'll make himself sick.

106
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:49,469
- Here. Slow, slow.
- <i>Then, after that,</i>

107
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:51,512
<i>they were trying to send him home,</i>

108
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,639
<i>but Sang-beom wouldn't go.</i>

109
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:55,933
<i>He clung to his brother instead.</i>

110
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:59,312
Seung-beom.
Why do you have to keep staying here?

111
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:01,772
You know how bad Mom
misses you at home, right?

112
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:05,985
So, why are you staying?
Come on. Let's go, come on!

113
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:07,111
- Hey, Beom.
- Shh!

114
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,197
Beom.

115
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,534
Do you know what having conviction means?

116
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:15,828
What's that?

117
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:18,414
I don't know anything about that stuff.

118
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,503
I'm really glad you don't, buddy.

119
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:26,923
I'm really, really glad.

120
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:32,386
Seung… Why are you even doing this, huh?

121
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:35,223
This is what college students
and politicians go and do!

122
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,017
I do know that much.

123
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:41,896
People like us, who didn't even
go to school and are poor,

124
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:44,106
who barely even know anybody,
we wouldn't do…

125
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,819
Yeah, exactly.

126
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:53,199
When you see people like us, who are poor,

127
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:55,618
uneducated, with no big, powerful friends.

128
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:02,166
What do you think drove
all of us to come fight?

129
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:12,677
Take Sang-beom here,
and please look after him.

130
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:15,304
Beom!

131
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:16,764
- I'm staying with you.
- Beom.

132
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,140
- If you're not leaving…
- Just let go first.

133
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,684
- I'm staying here too!
- Let go and we'll talk.

134
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:22,228
- Hey, boys! Stop. Hey, watch it!
- Beom, stop, let go. Beom, stop it!

135
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:23,437
Beom!

136
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:25,147
- Hey! Let go of that!
- Hey!

137
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,483
Hey, kid! Let it go!

138
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:32,280
Huh? It doesn't fire?

139
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:46,961
How are you gonna fight
if your gun won't shoot?

140
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,381
What are you doing, Seung-beom?

141
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:54,719
I'm not leaving you here.

142
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:59,390
If you stay in this place,
then I'm staying, too!

143
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,976
Beom, come on.

144
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,436
Oh, just stop it already, huh?

145
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:07,148
<i>Fellow citizens,</i>
<i>the martial law troops are storming in!</i>

146
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:10,610
<i>Our beloved brothers and sisters</i>
<i>are dying one by one</i>

147
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:12,695
<i>- at the hands of the martial law troops!</i>
- <i>I guess he figured</i>

148
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:14,739
<i>it wouldn't be safe to let him leave now.</i>

149
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:16,574
<i>Fight</i>
<i>the martial law troops to the bitter end!</i>

150
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:18,451
<i>And then he saw it.</i>

151
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:21,912
<i>Hell.</i>

152
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:31,047
- Mr. Oh! Hey, it's okay!
- Mr. Oh Sang-beom!

153
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,840
Look at me! Mr. Oh!

154
00:10:32,923 --> 00:10:35,676
- Look at me. Breathe, breathe!
- Calm down.

155
00:10:38,387 --> 00:10:40,931
Get down!

156
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:44,143
Down! Get down! Quick, quick! Find cover!

157
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:53,861
Holy shit!
They're shooting, they're shooting!

158
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:55,154
Everybody down!

159
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:58,491
- Beom! Beom!
- Get down! Run!

160
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,451
Beom! Beom!

161
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,803
What kind of a lunatic smashes
a hospital window? For the love of God.

162
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:22,390
There's a drone live streaming
Ji Du-seok's room, it's total chaos.

163
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:25,267
I'm just so relieved
Doctor Gye wasn't seriously hurt.

164
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,204
You wanted to die, didn't you?

165
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:48,874
With the surgery.

166
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,168
You didn't agree to it so you'd live,

167
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:52,962
you wanted to die.

168
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,132
Huh?

169
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:58,843
Sang-beom, is it true, what she said?

170
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:04,640
"What could I say to this man
in order to get him to agree to this?

171
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:07,184
What in the world can I do
to get this man…

172
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:11,439
who's only living to die,
to agree to live?"

173
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,443
Failure's a possibility.

174
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,573
If we fail, you will die.

175
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:26,787
<i>You gambled your life</i>
<i>a life you couldn't end yourself,</i>

176
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,789
<i>because you're living</i>
<i>in someone else's shoes.</i>

177
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,208
<i>A gamble on surgery</i>
<i>that could end in failure.</i>

178
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,295
I know what you were thinking.

179
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:38,716
I also know when you learned
the surgery may succeed,

180
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:41,135
you just couldn't bear the thought

181
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:45,306
of having to live the rest of your life
without ever seeing your brother again.

182
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:51,061
That can't be right.
That's your intention?

183
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:54,857
Did you just agree to the operation
for the chance you might die?

184
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:56,484
Except…

185
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:58,235
I will not let you.

186
00:12:58,319 --> 00:12:59,320
There's zero possibility.

187
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,573
I will make sure the surgery succeeds.

188
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:05,117
I can't stand here and let you throw away

189
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:07,036
a chance you've got
at living a better life.

190
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,423
You will get this surgery.

191
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:22,551
Why would you do that? Why?

192
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:23,969
You should live your life.

193
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:25,971
You need to keep going, son.

194
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,098
You need to try and live!

195
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:30,309
Sang-beom, you need to keep living!

196
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:32,019
You need to live!

197
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:51,413
So, how did you know?

198
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,249
That he was only living to die?

199
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:55,042
I know that look.

200
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,546
The look that says,

201
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:03,008
"Instead of me,
they should've gotten to live that day."

202
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:04,593
That look…

203
00:14:05,845 --> 00:14:08,013
that says,
"The only option I have is to live.

204
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,392
There's nothing left,
I'm just living to live."

205
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,770
Someone in endless torture…

206
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,565
while still being here.

207
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:23,279
Only that kinda person has that look.

208
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,909
Golly, I'm in for
a nice, smooth BM tomorrow.

209
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,414
We should let it go.

210
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,166
He said he doesn't want to.

211
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,169
Dr. Woo said he'd take him home,
so that's that.

212
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:41,922
We did everything we could.

213
00:14:42,673 --> 00:14:45,551
That man's just going to
fall apart if this goes on.

214
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:46,844
Even more than now.

215
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:54,393
When I grabbed him on the rooftop,
this thought came into my mind.

216
00:14:55,352 --> 00:14:57,396
"How does someone
get through this kind of a thing?

217
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:01,483
"Even if the surgery goes well, too…

218
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:05,863
…are any of us able to say he would
truly be living a better life afterwards?"

219
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,240
And, "What if…

220
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:11,493
he goes somewhere high, or goes and
takes another shot at doing this again?"

221
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,039
Oh, lord.

222
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,416
I guess I'm not helping much,
saying all this, am I?

223
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,711
In the case it goes well,
he's still barely hanging on here.

224
00:15:21,545 --> 00:15:24,548
What can any of us do to save
someone so desperate to die?

225
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,012
YOGURT DRINK

226
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:39,271
I wish you'd get diarrhea,
you constipated jerk!

227
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:40,606
Oh, goodness, you little…

228
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:43,108
- We're with doctors, have some manners.
- You've done it once already!

229
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:51,492
You helped me carry on.

230
00:16:05,589 --> 00:16:06,799
Doctor Gye, wait a minute!

231
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:10,636
If the surgery goes how we want,

232
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,596
do you think,
maybe it would heal his heart?

233
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,975
It will, won't it?
You'll make sure of it, right?

234
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:18,978
Because, honestly, I'm at a total loss.

235
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:21,939
I don't know what's best for him
or what's the right thing to do.

236
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,816
I feel completely useless here.

237
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,402
I just hope, that…

238
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:27,945
I just hope that he'll be able to rest

239
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:30,239
and finally get himself
a good night's sleep.

240
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:33,659
Doctor Gye, I'm sure
you know a way to help, right?

241
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,828
A procedure or something, right?

242
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,405
<i>I need to think.</i>

243
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:38,283
<i>I need to think harder. I need to find it.</i>

244
00:18:39,034 --> 00:18:41,995
<i>If I'm just able to</i>
<i>find a way for me to operate,</i>

245
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:44,581
<i>to get in there and remove it,</i>

246
00:18:45,791 --> 00:18:47,334
<i>then there's a real chance.</i>

247
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,837
<i>A doctor at the hospital</i>

248
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,172
<i>told the soldiers who were about to</i>
<i>take Mr. Oh Sang-beom away…</i>

249
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,465
GUNSHOT-INDUCED PENETRATING HEAD TRAUMA

250
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:55,884
<i>…"There's a bullet lodged in his head."</i>

251
00:18:56,468 --> 00:18:58,345
Do it, shoot it now! Quickly!

252
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:01,348
<i>Asleep or awake,</i>
<i>you'd ask for your brother.</i>

253
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:05,686
<i>You were sleeping, and you woke up</i>
<i>and you were sobbing, and saying,</i>

254
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,020
<i>"It's too heavy."</i>

255
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:10,524
<i>You'd say it over and over,</i>
<i>"It's too heavy. It's too heavy."</i>

256
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:18,282
Look who it is!

257
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:24,246
Doctor Gye Su-jeong,
Mr. Oh Sang-beom's primary surgeon.

258
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:25,873
Heading home for the day, eh?

259
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,499
Then again,
I wouldn't stay here late either,

260
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,710
if I knew the patient
was set to get transferred.

261
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:32,462
You didn't know? Really?

262
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:36,091
For him being in your care
and all that ruckus you caused over it,

263
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:37,843
you sure don't keep tabs.

264
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:39,720
Your surgery has been denied.

265
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:42,055
Come on, all right, all right,
no point arguing.

266
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:43,765
Don't bother with this temp doctor.

267
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:48,270
What is it? What?

268
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:50,147
Gonna pull another stunt?

269
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:52,816
Who are you?

270
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,026
Oh, God.

271
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:02,492
- Hey.
- Hey!

272
00:20:02,576 --> 00:20:04,453
- You little… What'd you just say?
- Hey!

273
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:06,663
Think you're some hot-shot?
Who do you think you are?

274
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,957
I think we're ready, Mr. Oh.
Let's get you home again.

275
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,001
- Wait, does she not recognize me?
- Of course she does.

276
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:13,837
- No, we met the other day! Hey!
- Please calm down, sir, okay?

277
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:15,756
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

278
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,098
Hey, get outta here.

279
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,352
I'm Macbeth.

280
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:33,148
Macbeth. Ah! Ah!

281
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:35,984
Ah, I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
Ah, I'm sorry, I'm sorr…

282
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:38,862
Hey, but wha…
Ah, it's cold, what was that?

283
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,072
You did drama in school?

284
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:42,658
Yes.

285
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:48,080
Yes?

286
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:55,254
DIRECTOR BU SEUNG-GWON

287
00:20:57,798 --> 00:20:58,799
Go on.

288
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:51,268
Dr. Gye, Dr. Jo, intern Park Tae-gyeong,

289
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:53,145
and Dr. Kim Seong-jin,

290
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:56,648
I'm going to need you all
to explain exactly what's going on here.

291
00:21:56,732 --> 00:22:01,361
Ms. Jang asked me to follow her here,
so I obliged that request, but…

292
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:20,589
On that day, when you were a child,

293
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:22,632
that night…

294
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:25,552
that moment 46 years ago.

295
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:27,637
We'd like to show everyone here

296
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:30,807
what we, through our research,
believe actually happened that night.

297
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,268
Uh, please have a seat, sir.

298
00:22:33,352 --> 00:22:35,103
It's okay, don't worry. It's okay.

299
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:36,772
All you'll need to do is sit and watch.

300
00:22:39,566 --> 00:22:41,693
They're going to reenact it as a play.

301
00:22:44,237 --> 00:22:45,572
We located

302
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:48,575
a room that matches
the original scene of the incident,

303
00:22:48,658 --> 00:22:49,993
as closely as it reasonably can.

304
00:22:50,577 --> 00:22:52,788
Down to the windows, their size,

305
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:54,748
the ceiling height, and the room width.

306
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:59,211
According to several witness accounts from
that day, at around 4:00 that morning,

307
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:01,546
a helicopter with a machine gun
started shooting

308
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:04,383
at the windows on the eighth floor
of the Gwangil Building.

309
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:08,637
In that room at the time,
were a 12-year old child, Sang-beom,

310
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:14,226
his 20-year-old brother, Seung-beom,

311
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:17,437
the restaurant owner,

312
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:20,232
the uncle to the two brothers,

313
00:23:24,319 --> 00:23:26,029
and the uncle to the two brothers.

314
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,827
Uncle, step forward.

315
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,331
And Seong-beom's friend…

316
00:23:38,166 --> 00:23:40,085
who he met at a night-school class.

317
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,422
The early-morning resistance broadcast
rings out,

318
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:45,590
and the group, fearing for their lives,

319
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,926
rushes inside the building
and takes cover.

320
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:52,013
But they didn't know that a helicopter
with a machine gun was deployed,

321
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:54,266
and would start shooting
straight through their windows.

322
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:04,025
They hear the sound of the helicopter.

323
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:06,611
The sound gets closer and closer,
and at that moment…

324
00:24:08,029 --> 00:24:10,157
they see the helicopter
through the window.

325
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:14,286
The group tries to run away…

326
00:24:15,745 --> 00:24:17,998
but a hail of bullets
is already raining down.

327
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:19,332
And those bullets…

328
00:24:37,309 --> 00:24:38,894
The older brother

329
00:24:38,977 --> 00:24:41,229
<i>covers his younger brother</i>
<i>with his whole body.</i>

330
00:24:43,315 --> 00:24:44,900
Beom! Beom!

331
00:25:00,123 --> 00:25:03,793
However, his older brother alone
couldn't protect him.

332
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:05,337
Then, then…

333
00:25:06,129 --> 00:25:07,464
if it wasn't just his brother…

334
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:10,550
One more person.

335
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:15,514
And…

336
00:25:20,810 --> 00:25:22,395
another, like this.

337
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:27,400
<i>The restaurant owner,</i>
<i>who was like a mother to him,</i>

338
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:31,780
his friend,

339
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:36,451
and then his friend's uncle.

340
00:25:39,412 --> 00:25:40,622
<i>Toward the child.</i>

341
00:25:42,749 --> 00:25:44,376
And after that…

342
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:39,598
Hey, look what I got.

343
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:41,766
Oh!

344
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:43,745
<i>No matter how hard I thought</i>
<i>on it, I couldn't make sense of it.</i>

345
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:46,998
<i>Even if it was old, it was still</i>
<i>a helicopter with a machine gun.</i>

346
00:27:47,082 --> 00:27:49,417
How is it that any of you
could've survived in there?

347
00:27:50,877 --> 00:27:52,128
"It's heavy."

348
00:27:53,046 --> 00:27:54,381
I heard you kept saying that,

349
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:56,675
in the first hospital you were in
after the incident.

350
00:27:58,677 --> 00:27:59,678
So I thought,

351
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:01,638
"Perhaps his brother, wasn't

352
00:28:02,347 --> 00:28:05,600
the only unbearable weight
that boy had to feel on that day."

353
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:18,113
Oh, Sang-beom, here.

354
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,256
Did you actually know?

355
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:41,678
Did the thought of what it was
ever occur to you?

356
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,522
It…

357
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:54,858
was…

358
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:04,659
It was so hea…

359
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:11,750
…heavy…

360
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:14,711
It was…

361
00:29:21,217 --> 00:29:24,721
It was… too… heavy to… hold.

362
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:34,147
It… was… too…

363
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,243
too… much… to…

364
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,879
It was… heavy… inside.

365
00:30:13,937 --> 00:30:15,897
So, would you like any…

366
00:30:16,689 --> 00:30:19,108
sounds or anything,
or some music playing in there,

367
00:30:19,192 --> 00:30:20,985
during your surgery today?

368
00:30:22,153 --> 00:30:23,738
You'll be under anesthesia, of course,

369
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:27,200
but we wanna do our best to make sure
you feel comfortable during surgery.

370
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:42,257
TRÄUMEREI

371
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,259
Mm… Okay.

372
00:30:56,229 --> 00:30:59,274
MY BROTHER LIKED THAT PIECE

373
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:07,365
Okay.

374
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:23,339
<i>You only get to die once.</i>

375
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:25,633
<i>So, save it for later.</i>

376
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:27,510
Take it slow.

377
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:30,680
Until tomorrow, then keep going.

378
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:32,682
Put it off.

379
00:31:33,182 --> 00:31:34,434
Just keep putting it off.

380
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:40,231
You'll make it where you need to go,

381
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:42,483
I will ensure you get there,
with your brother.

382
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:44,235
No matter what.

383
00:31:46,946 --> 00:31:48,114
Don't worry,

384
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:49,407
you can trust that.

385
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,118
It's not my nature to fail.

386
00:32:12,347 --> 00:32:15,558
His vitals are stable, and
he seems to be doing pretty well today.

387
00:32:36,496 --> 00:32:38,039
Can Dr. Gye pull this off?

388
00:33:06,484 --> 00:33:08,820
Patient name, Oh Sang-beom.

389
00:33:08,903 --> 00:33:12,323
Endoscopic foreign body removal
from right cerebral hemisphere.

390
00:33:12,407 --> 00:33:13,574
We will now begin.

391
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:49,819
MAY 18 OLD CEMETERY

392
00:34:26,981 --> 00:34:27,982
Sheath, please.

393
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:30,568
SHEATH: A SHORT TUBE THAT FACILITATES
VASCULAR ACCESS FOR CATHETERS & GUIDEWIRES

394
00:34:35,656 --> 00:34:36,741
Endoscope, please.

395
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:46,417
<i>Caught in a storm </i>

396
00:34:46,501 --> 00:34:50,463
<i>They all disappeared </i>

397
00:34:53,257 --> 00:34:54,592
- Hell yeah!
- Hell yeah!

398
00:35:02,141 --> 00:35:03,476
Cheers, brother.

399
00:35:38,386 --> 00:35:39,428
She found it.

400
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:48,896
Sang-beom.

401
00:35:50,773 --> 00:35:51,774
Sang-beom.

402
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:55,153
Hey, get up, buddy.

403
00:35:57,196 --> 00:35:58,281
We'll sleep after we eat.

404
00:36:01,075 --> 00:36:02,660
Gotta keep your strength.

405
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:12,920
Biopsy forceps.

406
00:36:13,004 --> 00:36:16,340
BIOPSY FORCEPS: ENDOSCOPIC FORCEPS
USED TO COLLECT TISSUE SAMPLES FOR BIOPSY

407
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:28,561
When I ask you
for biopsy forceps, leave the OR.

408
00:36:28,644 --> 00:36:31,272
- What? But I should wrap up--
- Stand at the end of the hall.

409
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,150
Okay.

410
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:38,571
Not gonna ask why?

411
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:40,072
I won't ask or argue back.

412
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:43,242
So, I'll leave
and stand at the end of the hall.

413
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:46,287
I'll do it.

414
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,485
Beom, hey.

415
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:20,821
Take care of yourself.

416
00:37:22,615 --> 00:37:23,908
Make sure you eat well,

417
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:29,622
and that you stay strong.

418
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:36,128
You should stay a little longer.

419
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:09,221
Huh? Is that a bullet?

420
00:39:09,305 --> 00:39:10,556
What is that?

421
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:13,100
- I couldn't see. Was it big?
- What is it?

422
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:26,113
- Huh? Let me see.
- Just… Just a moment.

423
00:39:26,906 --> 00:39:29,116
- Oh, good grief.
- Is that really it?

424
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:31,535
- Is that really a bullet?
- There's no way.

425
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:34,413
Uh, yeah, yeah, I think it is.

426
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:35,539
But, uh…

427
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:37,124
- I can't see it.
- Huh?

428
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:38,501
The bullet, uh… I…

429
00:40:38,269 --> 00:40:40,104
OPERATING ROOM

430
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:48,779
- What is it? Is it really a bullet?
- Uh, Doctor--

431
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:50,781
Doesn't look like a bullet. What is it?

432
00:40:51,949 --> 00:40:53,117
What'd you take out?

433
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,910
Give us the object, right now, Doctor.

434
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:56,912
Doctor Gye, was it really a bullet?

435
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:59,081
Come on, there's no reason
for you to keep it like that.

436
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:13,053
Park Tae-gyeong!

437
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:15,848
Huh? Uh… Yes, Doctor, I'm here!
I'm right over here!

438
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:19,977
- Huh? Huh?
- Hey, hey, hey, hey!

439
00:41:20,060 --> 00:41:21,937
No, no, no, no, no!

440
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,153
Now, run.

441
00:41:30,321 --> 00:41:32,490
- Yep!
- Doctor Gye, what the hell!

442
00:41:32,573 --> 00:41:35,075
- Have you lost your mind? Get back here!
- Tae-gyeong!

443
00:41:35,159 --> 00:41:36,660
- Hey!
- Park Tae-gyeong!

444
00:41:38,162 --> 00:41:40,956
What the hell! Park Tae-gyeong!

445
00:41:44,627 --> 00:41:47,546
You're still here. I knew
you wouldn't go chasing after him.

446
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:49,298
I only approved the surgery

447
00:41:49,381 --> 00:41:51,717
on the strict understanding
that it was a bullet.

448
00:41:53,302 --> 00:41:56,347
But I don't think I told anyone
that it was a bullet.

449
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:01,352
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

450
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:08,442
The vial you took from the OR,

451
00:42:09,109 --> 00:42:11,237
the one you still have
in your pocket right now,

452
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:13,322
does it contain what I'm suspecting?

453
00:42:14,573 --> 00:42:16,075
Well, what do you think it is, Director?

454
00:42:17,952 --> 00:42:19,578
It's a bone fragment.

455
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:28,420
I assure you that everybody will hear
of the lie you told about this.

456
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:41,058
Wait for Ms. Jang at gate three.
She'll be there soon.

457
00:42:42,393 --> 00:42:44,770
I didn't know you were capable of bribes.

458
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:49,483
Aren't you gonna change?

459
00:42:54,738 --> 00:42:56,907
Uh-oh, they look really mad.

460
00:42:56,991 --> 00:42:58,117
That's her, isn't it?

461
00:42:58,200 --> 00:42:59,785
- Hey, Doctor Gye.
- It is Gye Su-jeong!

462
00:42:59,868 --> 00:43:01,537
You know what you're
doing right now, don't you?

463
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:03,038
Come here!

464
00:43:03,122 --> 00:43:04,665
- The grunt work?
- Get over here!

465
00:43:04,748 --> 00:43:06,959
The night shift.
You're on the night shift.

466
00:43:07,042 --> 00:43:09,336
Never thought you'd purposely
work at night, Doctor, I'm shocked.

467
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:11,422
- Stop!
- Hey!

468
00:43:11,505 --> 00:43:13,007
Go get her, right now!

469
00:43:13,090 --> 00:43:14,216
God, that little…

470
00:43:16,468 --> 00:43:17,803
Doctor, wait!

471
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:20,931
You've got a real knack
for running, buddy.

472
00:43:21,015 --> 00:43:23,684
You and I both've been running
a little too much lately, haven't we?

473
00:43:23,767 --> 00:43:24,768
You're right.

474
00:43:27,104 --> 00:43:29,273
Oh. Is that her car?

475
00:43:29,356 --> 00:43:30,399
All right…

476
00:43:32,776 --> 00:43:35,154
- Just a second.
- Ah, can you open your…

477
00:43:35,237 --> 00:43:37,615
your window?

478
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:39,783
Just… just go up, through here.

479
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:41,327
- Here you go.
- Got it.

480
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:43,078
I appreciate all your help, Doctor.

481
00:43:43,162 --> 00:43:44,663
- Okay, good night!
- Good night.

482
00:43:46,707 --> 00:43:48,584
- Oh, my.
- Oh, uh, hello, Director.

483
00:43:48,667 --> 00:43:49,668
Ah, hey…

484
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:52,838
Gye Su-jeong, you pain in the neck,
you ought to make some big money!

485
00:43:52,921 --> 00:43:54,923
I swear to God,
I'll make you pay every penny.

486
00:43:55,007 --> 00:43:56,967
- Good night, you two.
- Yeah, you too.

487
00:43:58,886 --> 00:44:00,220
You think she'll be okay?

488
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:03,140
Oh…

489
00:44:03,223 --> 00:44:05,851
It's a miracle they all managed
to not get hurt for so long.

490
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:17,071
It's no wonder
they were so pissed earlier.

491
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,947
Why'd she give you
an empty container like that?

492
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:21,158
What? It's not empty, Doctor Jo.

493
00:44:21,241 --> 00:44:23,410
- Well, it's actually full.
- Of what?

494
00:44:24,578 --> 00:44:25,788
Care.

495
00:44:25,871 --> 00:44:28,624
The care Doctor Gye gives
whenever she treats somebody.

496
00:44:28,707 --> 00:44:30,084
- Sincerity.
- Huh…

497
00:44:30,167 --> 00:44:32,795
You've been hanging
with Kim Seong-jin too much.

498
00:44:32,878 --> 00:44:34,630
That's exactly the kind of thing
he would say.

499
00:44:35,214 --> 00:44:36,715
Don't get close to that man.

500
00:44:36,799 --> 00:44:38,676
Ah! Hey, she used
my real, actual name earlier.

501
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:40,552
I think it's the first time,
and she screamed it!

502
00:44:40,636 --> 00:44:42,429
- But--
- Park Tae-gyeong!

503
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:43,889
Hey, Jo Won-jin!

504
00:44:43,972 --> 00:44:45,224
What? Why's he coming over here?

505
00:44:45,307 --> 00:44:47,851
He said we should throw
a wrap party for our play earlier,

506
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:49,603
- and asked where we're gonna--
- No, a wrap party? As if!

507
00:44:49,687 --> 00:44:52,231
- Hold on! You're going to the wrap party?
- Uh, no, that's not--

508
00:44:52,314 --> 00:44:55,067
- Right? Right? Huh? Come back! Come back!
- No, we're not, Doctor Kim! Doctor Kim!

509
00:44:55,150 --> 00:44:56,944
- Why are you following me?
- Party time!

510
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:10,499
<i>The results will be out soon.</i>

511
00:45:10,582 --> 00:45:13,001
<i>If you're wrong,</i>
<i>I'm not feeding you for two days.</i>

512
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:14,461
<i>No allowance, either.</i>

513
00:45:23,220 --> 00:45:25,431
I guess he's not having
any dreams tonight.

514
00:45:30,769 --> 00:45:32,855
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

515
00:45:33,981 --> 00:45:35,399
Test, test.

516
00:45:36,358 --> 00:45:39,278
What do you mean it wasn't a bullet?
God, what a mess.

517
00:45:39,361 --> 00:45:41,822
Is it really in good taste
to be holding a press conference?

518
00:45:41,905 --> 00:45:45,033
On the contrary, they said
this would make it look a lot sadder.

519
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:47,035
- Says who?
- Them.

520
00:45:47,619 --> 00:45:49,163
Isn't he still upstairs?

521
00:45:49,955 --> 00:45:51,457
Along with that other guy too?

522
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:05,471
Ah… I got this when
I went to a shop yesterday.

523
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:06,805
It's for you. Here.

524
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:20,861
Well, then, you made it to the other side.

525
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:25,032
Once we get through
the press conference today,

526
00:46:25,657 --> 00:46:28,035
we'll go home for real this time, okay?

527
00:47:00,442 --> 00:47:01,819
Do you not see him anymore?

528
00:47:15,290 --> 00:47:18,168
In any case, I'm glad we were able to
arrange this press conference.

529
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:22,714
Well, if it isn't a bullet,
we don't get any use out of it, frankly.

530
00:47:22,798 --> 00:47:24,883
I'm wondering
why we took it in the first place.

531
00:47:24,967 --> 00:47:27,469
I mean, if it was a bullet,
you would've immediately seen it.

532
00:47:27,553 --> 00:47:29,137
The X-ray would've lit up where it was.

533
00:47:29,221 --> 00:47:30,639
Why didn't you tell us before?

534
00:47:30,722 --> 00:47:33,517
I think, clearly,
so she could do the surgery.

535
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:36,770
She is completely obsessed with surgery,
that Gye Su-jeong or whatever.

536
00:47:36,854 --> 00:47:40,232
Doctor Gye's reasoning was not unlike
that of the doctors back then,

537
00:47:40,315 --> 00:47:43,777
who… might make a call to lie
to protect the patient.

538
00:47:45,404 --> 00:47:46,780
What are you talking about?

539
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:49,992
- Are you picking her side?
- Ah, no way, no.

540
00:47:50,075 --> 00:47:51,910
Dr. Gye was in the wrong,
she wasn't being honest.

541
00:47:51,994 --> 00:47:55,664
Man, what am I supposed to say
at the press conference later, huh?

542
00:47:55,747 --> 00:47:57,583
I'm gonna lose face over this!

543
00:47:57,666 --> 00:47:58,750
<i>If they had known</i>

544
00:47:58,834 --> 00:48:02,004
that it wasn't actually a bullet,
but instead was a bone fragment…

545
00:48:03,380 --> 00:48:05,716
would those loudmouths
have supported this surgery, or not?

546
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:10,929
Mr. Director, I have no interest
in shaping, or changing the world.

547
00:48:11,013 --> 00:48:12,389
That's not my responsibility.

548
00:48:13,265 --> 00:48:15,642
In truth, I am someone who…

549
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:19,146
doesn't just say "yes" or "no",
but instead, asks…

550
00:48:20,355 --> 00:48:21,356
"Why?"

551
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:24,526
To know why is to be a better doctor.

552
00:48:26,194 --> 00:48:27,237
"Why?"

553
00:48:30,198 --> 00:48:31,575
"Why?" Huh…

554
00:48:35,495 --> 00:48:36,538
Hello?

555
00:48:38,081 --> 00:48:39,708
Huh? But there's no way.

556
00:48:40,292 --> 00:48:43,211
Oh Sang-beom, are you sure?
You're saying he got out?

557
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:47,382
Wow, these trusty potatoes.

558
00:48:47,466 --> 00:48:49,176
In the days when I was back up North…

559
00:48:49,259 --> 00:48:51,678
…potatoes like these were our lifeline.

560
00:48:51,762 --> 00:48:54,348
Oh! Oh, it's Doctor Woo.

561
00:48:55,265 --> 00:48:56,391
Hello, Dr. Woo.

562
00:48:57,142 --> 00:48:59,770
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.
- I was meaning to call you anyway.

563
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:02,356
I'm sorry, what?

564
00:49:02,439 --> 00:49:03,732
Well, I just…

565
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:06,109
I just stepped out briefly
to use the bathroom.

566
00:49:06,193 --> 00:49:07,653
Yes, yes, he's gone.

567
00:49:07,736 --> 00:49:09,947
I'm telling you, he's not in his room!

568
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:12,366
That's right!

569
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:13,742
THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING
I'M SORRY

570
00:49:13,825 --> 00:49:15,243
Oh, this is…

571
00:49:38,225 --> 00:49:39,351
Dr. Gye, update!

572
00:49:40,644 --> 00:49:42,646
The roof was all clear,
so that's not a worry.

573
00:49:42,729 --> 00:49:44,231
God, that's such a relief.

574
00:49:44,314 --> 00:49:46,274
I checked the cameras,
he didn't show up at all.

575
00:49:46,817 --> 00:49:48,318
I'm pretty sure he's still inside.

576
00:49:50,112 --> 00:49:51,571
GWANGJU UPRISING VICTIM SURGERY RESULTS

577
00:49:51,655 --> 00:49:55,367
The tragedy of Gwangju City
is a horrid tragedy for everybody.

578
00:49:55,450 --> 00:49:58,912
The pain Gwangju City suffered
is a pain that all of us share.

579
00:49:58,996 --> 00:50:02,874
What was discovered during surgery,
that pointed shard of bone,

580
00:50:03,959 --> 00:50:07,254
is a piercing and strong symbol
capturing the details of that tragedy.

581
00:50:07,754 --> 00:50:09,172
The path of the bullet.

582
00:50:09,756 --> 00:50:12,801
Sorrow captured and fragmented,
and deeply embedded within.

583
00:50:12,884 --> 00:50:15,387
- We must not turn a blind eye to this!
- Ah, he's just a natural up there.

584
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:16,763
He's incredible, isn't he?

585
00:50:17,347 --> 00:50:19,391
He is excellent at commanding
the room, for sure.

586
00:50:19,891 --> 00:50:21,518
I'd say it worked out for the better.

587
00:50:21,601 --> 00:50:24,479
He wouldn't've been able to say all that
with Mr. Oh Sang-beom in the room.

588
00:50:24,563 --> 00:50:26,690
The media wouldn't have focused
on the mayor, either.

589
00:50:26,773 --> 00:50:28,692
…we can prevent such a tragedy…

590
00:50:28,775 --> 00:50:31,028
Mr. Director, regarding our statement,

591
00:50:31,737 --> 00:50:32,988
read as we agreed upon.

592
00:50:43,081 --> 00:50:44,124
Come on, hurry.

593
00:50:44,207 --> 00:50:46,543
He must be close somewhere!
He doesn't know his way around here.

594
00:50:46,626 --> 00:50:49,004
- Get in.
- It's safer if I take my car and follow.

595
00:50:49,087 --> 00:50:50,839
Yeah, I think I should just tail you.

596
00:50:50,922 --> 00:50:53,175
Get in already. Come on, hurry!

597
00:50:53,258 --> 00:50:55,969
Oh, Miss Jang, I…
Oh my God, this old thing…

598
00:50:56,053 --> 00:50:58,180
- Okay.
- Seat belts!

599
00:51:01,975 --> 00:51:04,269
Thank you, everybody.
Now, Mr. Bu Seung-gwon, our Director,

600
00:51:04,352 --> 00:51:07,147
will begin taking your questions
at this time.

601
00:51:08,065 --> 00:51:10,358
My goodness, they're so glad
to go up there and take all the credit,

602
00:51:10,442 --> 00:51:12,194
but leave the mess for the Director.

603
00:51:12,277 --> 00:51:13,320
Quiet.

604
00:51:13,403 --> 00:51:14,988
If they're gonna do it,
why not handle the whole thing?

605
00:51:15,072 --> 00:51:16,198
Why drag the Director into it?

606
00:51:16,281 --> 00:51:17,949
He knew he had to,
'cause the hospital needed it,

607
00:51:18,033 --> 00:51:19,201
so he just agreed to do it.

608
00:51:19,284 --> 00:51:22,454
Uh, to all the journalists here today,
thank you for joining us.

609
00:51:22,537 --> 00:51:26,875
I am the director of Guseo University
Medical Center, Bu Seung-gwon.

610
00:51:26,958 --> 00:51:28,960
I'll now take your questions.

611
00:51:30,253 --> 00:51:32,589
Mr. Oh Sang-beom isn't here,
so why was he left out?

612
00:51:32,672 --> 00:51:36,218
At the moment, he's still recovering
and should be resting up for now.

613
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:38,762
Yes?

614
00:51:38,845 --> 00:51:42,099
If it didn't show up as metal, well,
you had to know that it wasn't a bullet.

615
00:51:42,182 --> 00:51:43,558
So, why'd you still operate?

616
00:51:43,642 --> 00:51:45,852
There was also talk of you
transferring Mr. Oh Sang-beom

617
00:51:45,936 --> 00:51:48,355
to another hospital
because of Mr. Ji Du-seok.

618
00:52:19,052 --> 00:52:20,637
OBOK NOODLES

619
00:52:20,720 --> 00:52:23,348
Please give us an answer.
Why did you perform the surgery?

620
00:52:23,431 --> 00:52:26,351
The hospital had ordered an X-ray,
which did show

621
00:52:26,935 --> 00:52:31,064
that it was indeed a bone fragment,
and not a bullet as we were thinking.

622
00:52:31,606 --> 00:52:35,819
However, we couldn't let
something so deeply serious,

623
00:52:35,902 --> 00:52:39,322
that caused the patient suffering,
to be overlooked.

624
00:52:39,906 --> 00:52:43,869
To be frank, it was a risky surgery,
there are no two ways about it.

625
00:52:44,452 --> 00:52:46,413
Though, regardless, the incredible doctors

626
00:52:46,496 --> 00:52:48,832
at this branch of
Guseo University Medical Center,

627
00:52:48,915 --> 00:52:51,543
the Honorable Mayor,
Im Ho-seok, as you know.

628
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:55,088
Chairman Kim Chang-su
of the Seonam Medical Association,

629
00:52:55,172 --> 00:52:58,758
and Chairman of the Guseo Foundation,
Gu Bon-pyeong,

630
00:52:58,842 --> 00:53:02,179
were all determined and intent
in the decision to operate.

631
00:53:03,680 --> 00:53:05,807
Miss Jang,
are you really not gonna take it?

632
00:53:05,891 --> 00:53:08,143
Get those out of here
before I change my mind.

633
00:53:08,226 --> 00:53:11,104
Don't charge for surgery
'cause it isn't what you thought.

634
00:53:11,188 --> 00:53:12,689
It doesn't matter that it's not a bullet.

635
00:53:12,772 --> 00:53:14,482
Just make sure,
after all he's been through…

636
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:16,776
he doesn't pay the bill.

637
00:53:19,946 --> 00:53:21,531
What's your reason behind this?

638
00:53:22,324 --> 00:53:23,992
There's a saying I heard recently,

639
00:53:24,075 --> 00:53:26,953
"Strive to be the salt of the earth."

640
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,872
I never want anyone to think I'm not.

641
00:53:29,581 --> 00:53:32,334
"Salt of the earth"? "Good character"?

642
00:53:32,918 --> 00:53:34,586
Gentlemen.

643
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:37,756
Ah, this is shitty!

644
00:53:37,839 --> 00:53:40,342
Damn it! I really wanted to get a new car.

645
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:44,429
You have it?

646
00:53:45,805 --> 00:53:46,973
Right here.

647
00:53:47,057 --> 00:53:49,017
Huh? That's Mr, Oh Sang-beom's
bone fragment

648
00:53:49,100 --> 00:53:51,686
- I gave you the other day-- What?
- No, it's not.

649
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:53,438
It wasn't from Mr. Oh, actually.

650
00:53:55,649 --> 00:53:57,609
Oh! Oh! There, there, there!
It's Oh Sang-beom!

651
00:53:57,692 --> 00:53:58,944
- He's over there!
- What? Where?

652
00:53:59,027 --> 00:54:01,988
Oh! I think he just went down that alley.

653
00:54:02,948 --> 00:54:06,618
<i>Mr. Oh Sang-beom, at the time,</i>
<i>was only twelve years old.</i>

654
00:54:07,202 --> 00:54:10,247
<i>As I imagine, when martial law forces</i>
<i>came and tried to take him away,</i>

655
00:54:10,330 --> 00:54:12,123
<i>the doctor who was in charge then,</i>

656
00:54:12,207 --> 00:54:16,086
had decided to tell a small, white lie,

657
00:54:16,169 --> 00:54:17,963
to protect his patient.

658
00:54:18,046 --> 00:54:21,341
And later, when a fire destroyed
Mr. Oh's medical records,

659
00:54:21,424 --> 00:54:23,385
that lie became the truth.

660
00:54:24,886 --> 00:54:29,224
This hospital made a choice
and admitted Mr. Oh, and Mr. Ji Du-seok,

661
00:54:29,307 --> 00:54:32,352
because after all,
both gentlemen are patients.

662
00:54:32,435 --> 00:54:36,189
In no event did we ever consider
transferring them to another hospital.

663
00:54:36,273 --> 00:54:38,275
Like the doctors did in those days,

664
00:54:38,358 --> 00:54:40,527
we, at our hospital, all…

665
00:54:41,278 --> 00:54:42,946
share the same principle,

666
00:54:43,029 --> 00:54:46,449
uh, and sentiment that
all doctors should share.

667
00:54:47,826 --> 00:54:51,121
TO UPHOLD OUR OBLIGATIONS
WITH A "WHITE-COAT" SENSE OF DUTY

668
00:54:52,706 --> 00:54:53,999
A white sense.

669
00:54:57,711 --> 00:55:01,047
- Uh, that is a sense of duty--
- <i>Code blue. Code blue.</i>

670
00:55:01,131 --> 00:55:03,425
- "Code blue"?
- <i>Room five, VIP ward, third floor.</i>

671
00:55:03,508 --> 00:55:06,052
<i>- Cardiology, cardiothoracic surgery.</i>
- What is it?

672
00:55:06,136 --> 00:55:07,721
- I didn't get a… Oh.
<i>- Code Blue, Code Blue.</i>

673
00:55:07,804 --> 00:55:10,056
<i>- Room five, VIP ward, third floor.</i>
- What?

674
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:12,142
<i>- Cardiology and cardiothoracic surgery.</i>
- Wait a second. Who…

675
00:55:12,225 --> 00:55:13,560
Did you just get this too?

676
00:55:13,643 --> 00:55:14,644
Ji Du-seok?

677
00:55:14,728 --> 00:55:16,479
- Ji Du-seok?
- Ji Du-seok?

678
00:55:16,563 --> 00:55:18,940
That Code Blue, it's Ji Du-seok!
That Code Blue, it's Ji Du-seok!

679
00:55:19,024 --> 00:55:20,817
Is ex-president Ji Du-seok
the reason for that?

680
00:55:20,900 --> 00:55:22,152
Ah, everyone, just…

681
00:55:22,235 --> 00:55:25,071
- just let me finish, let me say--
- Isn't Code Blue for cardiac arrest?

682
00:55:25,155 --> 00:55:26,990
Are you sure your initial
response was sufficient?

683
00:55:27,073 --> 00:55:29,075
- Let me finish first--
- Can you confirm it's Mr. Ji Du-seok?

684
00:55:29,159 --> 00:55:30,618
Can you confirm whether
he was conscious during transport?

685
00:55:30,702 --> 00:55:31,536
What was the cause?

686
00:55:31,619 --> 00:55:33,330
It'd be best to clear the stage, Director.

687
00:55:33,413 --> 00:55:34,831
- Come on.
- When did his condition become critical?

688
00:55:34,914 --> 00:55:37,625
I can explain the matter
in detail shortly.

689
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:39,878
I'll brief you about this matter
when we're ready.

690
00:55:39,961 --> 00:55:41,171
Please say a few words!

691
00:55:41,254 --> 00:55:43,757
Was there an injury that
caused a sudden change in his condition?

692
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:45,967
Is Mr. Ji Du-seok in critical condition?

693
00:55:47,344 --> 00:55:48,720
Don't you wanna go look?

694
00:55:48,803 --> 00:55:50,597
No, this has
nothing to do with me, so I'll stay.

695
00:55:56,728 --> 00:55:58,688
Well, he went into a karaoke joint.

696
00:55:58,772 --> 00:56:01,066
And bought something
at a convenience store.

697
00:56:01,149 --> 00:56:02,984
It was in a black plastic bag,
so I couldn't get a look,

698
00:56:03,068 --> 00:56:04,444
but I'm starting to worry.

699
00:56:23,296 --> 00:56:26,007
You found him! Okay! Woo-hoo!

700
00:56:26,091 --> 00:56:28,259
Ah! Now there you are, at last!

701
00:56:29,302 --> 00:56:31,888
Quite the exciting place you came to.
Hey, get in here!

702
00:56:31,971 --> 00:56:33,765
All right, all right, let's choose a song!

703
00:56:33,848 --> 00:56:35,809
I'll go first, if nobody else minds.

704
00:56:35,892 --> 00:56:37,102
Press the button after me.

705
00:56:37,185 --> 00:56:39,229
Okay, here we go.

706
00:56:39,312 --> 00:56:44,067
Ah, four, five, one, seven. And start!

707
00:56:53,201 --> 00:56:54,369
<i>Breaking news.</i>

708
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:58,039
<i>Former President Ji Du-seok passed away</i>
<i>at 11:45 a.m. this morning,</i>

709
00:56:58,123 --> 00:56:59,749
<i>at the age of 91.</i>

710
00:57:00,834 --> 00:57:04,921
<i>Former President Ji, whose health</i>
<i>had been declining rapidly in recent days,</i>

711
00:57:05,004 --> 00:57:08,216
<i>was receiving treatment at a hospital</i>
<i>when his condition suddenly worsened,</i>

712
00:57:08,299 --> 00:57:11,261
<i>later unfortunately succumbing</i>
<i>to cardiac arrest.</i>

713
00:57:12,429 --> 00:57:14,639
<i>The medical community mourns his passing.</i>

714
00:57:15,223 --> 00:57:20,603
<i>A rocky island where the waves crash</i>

715
00:57:21,271 --> 00:57:25,817
<i>In this desolate place</i>

716
00:57:26,693 --> 00:57:32,490
<i>The people of the world, one by one</i>

717
00:57:34,075 --> 00:57:38,246
<i>Gathered together</i>

718
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:45,837
<i>But one night, caught in a storm</i>

719
00:57:47,088 --> 00:57:50,967
<i>They all disappeared</i>

720
00:57:52,927 --> 00:57:54,554
I couldn't tell you before your surgery,

721
00:57:54,637 --> 00:57:57,891
since I'd been waiting
for the results of the DNA test.

722
00:58:03,188 --> 00:58:05,648
This bone fragment
is actually your brother's.

723
00:58:13,031 --> 00:58:16,075
All this time, what was in your head…

724
00:58:17,535 --> 00:58:18,661
was your brother.

725
00:58:19,913 --> 00:58:20,955
He…

726
00:58:21,789 --> 00:58:23,208
was always with you.

727
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:31,299
Hey, Seung.

728
00:58:32,592 --> 00:58:33,843
It's okay.

729
00:58:35,970 --> 00:58:37,430
Let's go home again.

730
00:58:41,559 --> 00:58:42,602
Together.

731
00:59:23,059 --> 00:59:24,978
<i>Yes, evidence has once again emerged</i>

732
00:59:25,061 --> 00:59:28,648
<i>that proves there was helicopter gunfire</i>
<i>during the Gwangju Democratic Uprising.</i>

733
00:59:29,274 --> 00:59:31,025
<i>There are accounts that</i>
<i>the Gwangil Building</i>

734
00:59:31,109 --> 00:59:33,319
<i>came under assault on the final day.</i>

735
00:59:34,112 --> 00:59:35,405
<i>Hundreds of bullet holes were found</i>

736
00:59:35,488 --> 00:59:38,032
<i>in the walls of a room</i>
<i>on the eighth floor of this building.</i>

737
00:59:38,116 --> 00:59:40,326
<i>The martial law troops at the time</i>

738
00:59:40,410 --> 00:59:41,828
<i>- cemented the holes and all traces…</i>
- Mommy!

739
00:59:41,911 --> 00:59:43,871
<i>…of armed suppression in the city,</i>

740
00:59:43,955 --> 00:59:47,250
<i>so it was difficult to find evidence</i>
<i>of the atrocities committed.</i>

741
00:59:48,042 --> 00:59:51,504
<i>However, because this room</i>
<i>was largely neglected after the uprising,</i>

742
00:59:51,588 --> 00:59:54,090
<i>the evidence appears</i>
<i>to have been preserved.</i>

743
00:59:54,173 --> 00:59:55,883
<i>- With this discovery…</i>
- Oh, Dr. Gye, over here.

744
00:59:55,967 --> 00:59:57,635
<i>…the families of those affected</i>
<i>have called for the state</i>

745
00:59:57,719 --> 01:00:00,221
<i>to investigate further.</i>
<i>The Commission to Investigate the truth</i>

746
01:00:00,305 --> 01:00:02,640
<i>of the May Eighteenth</i>
<i>Democratization Movement</i>

747
01:00:02,724 --> 01:00:06,060
<i>announced that it'll compare the records</i>
<i>of the rebels and the martial law forces.</i>

748
01:00:06,144 --> 01:00:08,229
<i>Breaking news,</i>
<i>the government has announced</i>

749
01:00:08,313 --> 01:00:10,148
<i>plans to increase</i>
<i>medical school enrollment.</i>

750
01:00:10,231 --> 01:00:11,941
- It's been confirmed?
- They're really going through with it?

751
01:00:12,025 --> 01:00:14,068
- This isn't the time for that.
- Man, this is bad.

752
01:00:14,152 --> 01:00:16,195
<i>The increase would raise enrollment</i>

753
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:18,865
<i>by more than 2000 students,</i>
<i>starting next year.</i>

754
01:00:19,490 --> 01:00:21,367
<i>The goal is to double</i>
<i>the previous admissions quota.</i>

755
01:00:21,451 --> 01:00:22,619
GOVERNMENT TO INCREASE
MED SCHOOL QUOTA BY 2,000

756
01:00:22,702 --> 01:00:26,164
<i>This new increase</i>
<i>is the first hike in 17 years,</i>

757
01:00:26,247 --> 01:00:31,502
<i>yet the policy was pushed through despite</i>
<i>opposition from the medical community.</i>

758
01:00:32,712 --> 01:00:34,297
<i>The Korean Medical Association</i>

759
01:00:34,380 --> 01:00:36,174
<i>immediately opposed the move,</i>

760
01:00:36,257 --> 01:00:38,134
<i>- warning that it would undermine…</i>
- You can eat this too.

761
01:00:38,217 --> 01:00:40,053
<i>…the quality of medical care</i>
<i>and fuel excessive competition.</i>

762
01:00:40,136 --> 01:00:43,598
<i>University hospitals across the country</i>
<i>also expressed regret over the decision.</i>

763
01:00:43,681 --> 01:00:47,226
<i>The Korean Intern Resident Association</i>
<i>and Korean Medical Association</i>

764
01:00:47,310 --> 01:00:49,395
<i>have called for all students</i>
<i>and doctors to go on strike…</i>

765
01:00:49,479 --> 01:00:51,481
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

766
01:01:31,437 --> 01:01:33,523
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

767
01:01:34,148 --> 01:01:37,485
All interns are to stop the execution
of their duties and exit the hospital.

768
01:01:37,568 --> 01:01:39,153
<i>Right now, as we're speaking,</i>

769
01:01:39,237 --> 01:01:40,738
<i>a 10-year-old's</i>
<i>getting her stomach kicked.</i>

770
01:01:41,322 --> 01:01:44,200
<i>If you're not going to remove it,</i>
<i>be decent enough to look the other way.</i>

771
01:01:44,283 --> 01:01:46,160
<i>How can you brand</i>
<i>those who stay behind as traitors,</i>

772
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:47,995
just because they want to
care for their patients?

773
01:01:48,079 --> 01:01:50,707
Come on, how can you even do this, huh?

774
01:01:50,790 --> 01:01:53,292
<i>They will take legal action</i>
<i>against medical professionals.</i>

775
01:01:53,376 --> 01:01:56,629
As doctors, we can't be expected
to just look the other way!

776
01:01:56,713 --> 01:01:58,673
If you're a doctor,
then help with the surgery.
